On K8s Master node if you see the below issue follow the steps to resolve it.
 
ISSUE:
[root@blt12393059 kubernetes]# kubectl get ns
error: You must be logged in to the server (Unauthorized)
[root@blt12393059 kubernetes]#
 
SOLUTION:
We need to copy admin.conf into the /root/.kube/ path. Take a backup of the existing config file, then move admin.conf as config and set the correct permissions.
 
PATH=$PATH:/etc/kubernetes
echo $PATH
locate .kube
cd /root/.kube
ls -lart
cd /etc/kubernetes
ls -lrth
cp admin.conf /root/.kube/
cd /root/.kube
cp config config_11012024
mv admin.conf config
chmod 755 config
 
